<title>USA: FDA panel backs Pharmacia smoking cessation aid.</title>
<headline>FDA panel backs Pharmacia smoking cessation aid.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A federal advisory committee on Friday recommended the Food and Drug Administration approve for marketing a Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn nicotine inhaler to help people stop smoking, the company said.</p>
<p>It said the FDA's Drug Abuse Advisory Committee voted to find the Nicotrol Inhaler both effective and safe as a smoking cessation aid. The FDA is not bound by the recommendations of its expert advisory panels, but usually accepts them.</p>
<p>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn said the inhaler will be marketed in the United States by McNeil Consumer Products, a unit of Johnson &amp; Johnson.</p>
</text>
